/-!
# Structurality from `Equation4424` through a two-guard companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell2.py`.  `Equation4424` is `x ◇ (x ◇ y) = (z ◇ z) ◇ y`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with `x □ y = if (M.op a a) = b then a else if (M.op b b) = b then a else (M.op b a)` is an automorphism of `◇` --
is `GuardAut2_pxx_y_pyy_y_x_x_pyx_Equation4424`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation names no target, so every
law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
are 4 of them below.
-/

